{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2420,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6600,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hello. Hey."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8440,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, this is good, this is good. You - you're working, can you see me?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12000,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can see you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13660,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you know what went wrong in-uh.. during the launch..?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15940,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes - it's not complicated, but, it's a long chain of events.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20800,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On august, 21., 2014, two satellites were launched by the European Space Agency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25860,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're called Galileo Satellites 5 and 6."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28840,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were intended to become part of the Global Navigation Satellite System, or GNSS."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33560,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the European version of the American GPS systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36340,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40680,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, after successfully blasting off into space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42780,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The satellites were launched with the Russian 5-6 rockets;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46400,
    "dDurationMs": 8040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The final stage of the rocket was set to inject the satellites into circular orbit around 23000 kilometers above the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54540,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that - - is when something went wrong"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57720,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uhh. there was thermal breach between a line of cold helium, and a line of propellant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64240,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the propellant, it froze;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66820,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This caused the failure of the altitude control thrusters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69720,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The satellites seemed to have been injected into some random direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73280,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was launched, but in the wrong direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76060,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This sent the satellites into highly elliptical, and seemingly useless orbits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80920,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At their low point, the satellites didn't really get a full view of earth.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83940,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Earth sensors, which enabled them to orient their navigation antennas - stopped working,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88880,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the earth just filled their field of view."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the other extreme, the satellites went too high, experiencing significant radiation exposure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97560,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "due to the van Allen belts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99000,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was a threat, that they would just shut them off.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103180,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, who do we have to talk to, to make sure they keep these satellites alive?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107500,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had an idea, for how to use them to make the best tests of general relativity to date;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113260,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was a strike of luck for us, we had been proposing such missions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116400,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we saw that this accident happened, we were very happy about it, of course."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119580,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the satellites did have propellant on board,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "intended to allow for periodic course corrections over their planned 10 year lifespan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127160,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127660,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they could use that fuel to attempt to correct their orbits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130700,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they used the propellant on board -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133265,
    "dDurationMs": 2590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They did some of these maneuvers to bring them into stable orbit -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135860,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they didn't have enough to completely turn their elliptical orbits into circular ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140940,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They couldn't circularize completely, thankfully for our project."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145860,
    "dDurationMs": 6780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to general relativity, relative to a reference clock, clocks tick slower in stronger gravitational fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152640,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is to say, closer to large masses, like the Earth, deeper in gravitational wells,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157580,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so, clocks in satellites should tick faster relative to those on Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161080,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they're in weaker gravitational fields"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163920,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164420,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, I'm ignoring the special relativistic effect that works the other way -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167660,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making clocks in satellites tick slower than those on Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170720,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they're moving so much faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172940,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This velocity effect is very well tested, so we focused on the gravitational parts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The gravitational effect is hard to measure precisely, for satellites in circular orbit,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182320,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but satellites in elliptical orbit, have an advantage - -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185800,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In every orbit -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186820,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they go from their lowest position - perigee,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189685,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the highest position - apogee, and back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192585,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to test the gravitational red-shift of a clock, you need two things - -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195325,
    "dDurationMs": 4695,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you need a very accurate clock, and you need a large change in gravitational potential."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200020,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The satellite goes from 17000 to 26000 kilometers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206380,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The difference in altitude is almost 9000 (!!!) kilometers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210440,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning they are rapidly, and repeatedly going from lower gravitational potential,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214580,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to higher gravitational potential, and back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216780,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So clocks on board, should be ticking slower when they're closer to the Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220600,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then faster when they go to their high point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223140,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they'll keep oscillating back and forth; slower and faster relative to clocks on Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228480,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228980,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you compare a clock on the ground, and a clock on the satellite,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233000,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you will have this variation of time.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236620,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, what's great about this, is it allows you to eliminate a lot of sources of error -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241560,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because, you don't really care about the absolute accuracy of the clocks;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245900,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All you want to know, is the difference between the rate of ticking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248980,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the low point compared to the high point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since it's the same clock making the measurements at both locations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255140,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can eliminate a lot of errors, like the noise in the clock, or a systematic drift,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260100,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's what allows the scientists to achieve such incredible precision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264680,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why we could do it - is because it's a very predictable effect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268380,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Due to the eccentricity of the orbit - the signal we were looking for, is really the modulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271960,
    "dDurationMs": 7260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All the other effects - that are at other periods - they will not have an influence on your measurements."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279220,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, I should point out, that if you were traveling with the satellite,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282880,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for you - time would not speed up and slow down; time would be passing at a constant rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288780,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You wouldn't be able to measure any change in the rate the clock is ticking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292380,
    "dDurationMs": 9700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The relativity comes when you compare two clocks which are distant enough to feel the curvature of space and time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The clocks on the satellites - there are a couple of different types - are all atomic clocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306800,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The primary clock typically is a passive hydrogen MASER clock."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310740,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A MASER - is just like a laser, except it uses microwaves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Atoms of hydrogen interact with one specific frequency of microwaves -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320220,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A photon of precisely this frequency, will flip the spin of an electron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324900,
    "dDurationMs": 560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325460,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by tuning the microwaves, so that they best interact with the hydrogen atoms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330360,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then counting up exactly this number of cycles of that radiation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334420,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's one second. You can keep track of time with incredible stability."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339240,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, over a 30 million years, a clock like this -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342500,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would not be out by more than a second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345900,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346400,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, if you were traveling with the satellite, you would always observe the frequency of this radiation to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351860,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same. But, if you sent this radiation out - -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354920,
    "dDurationMs": 505,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355425,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a distant observer -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357125,
    "dDurationMs": 2335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who is not in a strong gravitational field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359580,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would observe the frequency of your microwaves to be slightly lower than those from their hydrogen maser."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365700,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words - red-shifted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367840,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the closer the satellite is to Earth, the more red-shifted the microwaves would appear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372360,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And hence the slower time would pass, relative to that distant  observer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376820,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Locally, you can not see any relativistic effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381480,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called the equivalence principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383820,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's only when you compare the satellite clock to one on Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387540,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you would find the yo-yo-ing rate of the satellite's clock due to it's oscillation back and forth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392880,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Earth's gravitational well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395020,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This gravitational redshift was previously measured most precisely in 1976."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400900,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right, for over 40 years, we haven't improved our measurement of the gravitational effect on time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407020,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1976, Gravity Probe A was launched aboard a sub-orbital rocket -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411800,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it went up in a parabolic trajectory, reaching a maximum altitude of 10000 kilometers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417020,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then it came down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418500,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That gives you quite a lot of modulation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420640,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and gravitational potential."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421800,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The whole time it was in contact with the Earth, through the microwave signal of the on-board hydrogen maser."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427940,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then they did a direct frequency comparison, so they really did a two-way microwave link."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433140,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This allowed for a direct comparison of the rate of which a clock would tick on a rocket,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436980,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relative to a clock on Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The results matched the predictions of general relativity down to a 140 parts per million."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445120,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The scientists I'm talking to were eventually able to convince those in charge of the satellites,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449580,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to let them use their misfortune to test the gravitational redshift predictions of general relativity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455320,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But actually carrying out the tests, wasn't easy; one of the biggest sources of error was the positions of the satellites."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461640,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'd think, in the emptiness of space, the satellites would perfectly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465640,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maintain their orbits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467760,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that neglects the power of sunlight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470360,
    "dDurationMs": 7480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The photons of the sun, bouncing on the satellites, is the biggest source of error."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477840,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right, the momentum of photons hitting the satellites was enough to significantly impact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482660,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the measurements. Careful modeling plus laser ranging to the satellites, brought the orbital uncertainties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488280,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down to an acceptable level."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490420,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One way to improve the statistics was by collecting data over more than a thousand days."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493800,
    "dDurationMs": 2855,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's almost 3 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496655,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unlike Gravity Probe A, which spent only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499355,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2 hours in space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500395,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So .. what did they find?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504465,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that we both agree that we did not prove Relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507585,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There isn't that we confirm the General Relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511185,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513565,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were able to reduce the uncertainty in the measurement"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516615,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a factor of 5"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518735,
    "dDurationMs": 3130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over Gravity Probe A\nSo it's a new high score"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521865,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first in over 40 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524915,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what is the point?\nYou saying 'unfortunately'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528125,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529655,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know what we're looking for, is deviation from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532395,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "General Relativity. Because we know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535405,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is not the ultimate error."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538105,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "History has taught us that, new physics always lies at the boundaries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541155,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that more and more precise tests sometimes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544175,
    "dDurationMs": 3110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reveal brand new aspects of nature, that we never would've observed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547565,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if we had not made efforts to look"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550485,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there are good reasons to believe that General Relativity may not be the whole story"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553935,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both it and Quantum Mechanics are spectacularly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556955,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "successful theories in their own rights"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559795,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for nearly a century, all attempts to merge the two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562885,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have been more or less failures. Plus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565845,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our current"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567025,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "world view includes dark energy and dark matter which make up more than 90% of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570015,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything there is in the universe.\nThe fact that this is all down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573045,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is not understood, tells me that maybe, we don't know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575975,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything about gravity already.\nWhen more tests are planned"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579005,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to further prove the General Relativity and determine if there's a test it can pass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582905,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a cold cesium atom clock is set to fly in the international"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586025,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "space station and it aims to reduce the deviation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588955,
    "dDurationMs": 2830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a further factor of 10.\nAs for the satellites,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591785,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their orbits were made more circular using the propellants on board"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594685,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though they are still elliptical.\nThe navigation signals have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597575,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been tested and are within acceptable parameters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600615,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the moment, they are restricted to 'test mode'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603365,
    "dDurationMs": 3130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "awaiting some new software and modifications on the ground, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606495,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the hope is that they will be useful for navigation after all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609505,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in the meantime, they hold the record for achieving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612345,
